  "split_decision": "Separate the actual integer equality wrapper from its arbitrary flow-realization proposition wrapper. Preserve mixed own-provider transport/quasi-isomorphism records and all genuine proof terms in exact archives rather than invent a flow action, weaken a type or add a missing self-provider dependency.",
  "review_notes": [
    "The exact original RodgersTaoDerivedTransport stores an independently supplied heatFamily, source/target SectionComplex values, a genuinely indexed EulerPreservingTransport for those same complexes, and an arbitrary flowRealizesDerivedTransport proposition/proof plus label. No predicate relates heatFamily to eulerTransport.",
    "Both theorems are genuine proof content. The first projects the selected flow proposition; the second returns the actual targetEuler.value = sourceEuler.value equality already required by eulerTransport. Preserve both full arguments and proof bodies.",
    "The inspected heat-family source has zeroPosition : Time -> ZeroIndex -> Real, with unrelated backwardsHeatEquation and newmanLambdaNonnegative proposition/proof fields. It defines no heat differential equation or real Newman parameter in those fields; the theorem names do not supply those missing relations.",
    "The inspected Euler transport has an actual integer equality and degreewise map but arbitrary respectsDifferential/quasiIsoLike propositions. SectionComplex/EulerCharacteristic lack linked square-zero and Euler-sum equations. No analytic flow action, derived equivalence, cohomology invariant, probability/moment result or independent index construction follows from this package.",
    "Keep all three own-provider commands in exact GRWTSK archives. Extracting its consequence alone would add a legacy self-provider import absent from the original; copying a weakened record or claiming the actual equality was absent would also be wrong."
  ],
  "shared_attribution_record": "MATH-ATTRIBUTION-254"
